{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The excess on this trip is established but it is not MATERIAL. The governing trace figure is 10.13 km against the booked optimal of 7.40 km, an excess of 2.73 km — 36.89% of optimal. POL-RD-01 makes a deviation material only when the excess exceeds 50% of optimal OR exceeds 8.0 km absolute; neither is met here. Because the deviation is not material, POL-RD-06's driver_profile check is not engaged, and no repeat-pattern uplift, no FULL_REFUND uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral can follow from this trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00534", "EV-TRIP-00534"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even if the driver_profile is consulted, no repeat deviation pattern is ESTABLISHED under POL-RD-06. driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0, where the clause requires 3 or more; and deviation_flags_90d divided by completed_trips_90d (250) is 0.00, far below the 0.05 the clause requires. POL-RD-06 therefore yields nothing at all — not the balance-shift in limb (a), not the FULL_REFUND uplift in limb (b), and not the conduct referral in limb (c) — and POL-GEN-01 forbids substituting any other profile field (rating, account_age_days, lifetime_trips, prior_deviation_flags) for the two counters the clause actually names.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00534", "EV-GPS-00534"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The ceiling on any refund is the POL-RD-02 arithmetic, and it is modest. charged_total is 19.74; the recomputed optimal-route fare is ((3.80 + 0.75 x 7.4 + 0.28 x 13.0) x the 1.0 surge multiplier recorded on the fare_breakdown) + 0.80 platform fee = 13.79; refund = 19.74 - 13.79 = 5.95, which is 30.1% of the charge. A FULL_REFUND requires the refund to be 90% or more of charged_total under POL-RD-02, or a MATERIAL deviation substantiated on this trip's own evidence together with an established POL-RD-06 pattern; neither is present. The rider's demand for the whole 19.74 is unsupported, and would in any event return the 3.80 base fare and 0.80 platform fee that no clause refunds and that POL-RD-02's recomputation deliberately retains.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00534"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing is owed as a pass-through correction under POL-RD-09. The fare_breakdown itemises no ERP gantry lines (off-optimal-route ERP total 0.00, on-optimal-route total 0.00), no tolls, and no airport surcharge — and in any case a surcharge line would be improper here, since the trip neither originates nor terminates at an airport. There is accordingly no off-route or phantom line to refund standalone, and nothing may be added on top of the POL-RD-02 figure.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00534", "EV-GPS-00534"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver has no exculpatory clause on this record, and I do not stretch for one. The only traffic advisory is absent: EV-ADVIS-00534-01 is MISSING, its status is MISSING with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT and weight_multiplier 0.0, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run at all. The chat log EV-CHAT-00534 holds a single message, from the driver — 'setting off now' — with waypoint_hint null, so POL-RD-04's rider-instruction corroboration test is undecidable on the record rather than satisfied; the clause is simply unavailable, as it expressly provides where no waypoint and no named road exist. And no pickup or dropoff amendment is recorded (pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are both null), so POL-RD-05 does not apply. The excess therefore stands and the case is governed by the POL-RD-02 partial refund of 5.95.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00534-01", "EV-CHAT-00534", "EV-TRIP-00534"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-05", "POL-RD-02"]
    }
  ]
}
